{
 "summary": "Between about 00:12:47Z and 00:14:46Z, checkout requests failed intermittently with 502s at gateway, peaking at 22% of requests. The errors start in inventory: POST /reserve returned 500 while inventory logged 'connection reset by peer', and orders and gateway passed that failure up the chain. The failures were fast rather than timeouts, and the error ratio was back to 0 at the end of the window; which peer reset inventory's connections is not in the evidence.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Inventory's POST /reserve returned 500s because a connection inventory depends on was reset by its peer ('connection reset by peer', 44 occurrences). Orders turned these into 502s on POST /orders, and gateway turned those into 502s on POST /checkout. The peer and why it reset connections are not identified in the evidence.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-a54c7699226e",
   "ev-c30708431859",
   "ev-a57a947e1357",
   "ev-01577e4a4821",
   "ev-da66dff6a849"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Neither orders nor gateway absorbed the inventory failure. Orders logged 'inventory reservation failed with status 500' and gateway logged 'checkout failed: orders returned 502', 44 times each, matching inventory's 44 resets and sharing the same example traces.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-a57a947e1357",
    "ev-01577e4a4821",
    "ev-c30708431859"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "The failures were intermittent, not continuous: gateway's 5xx ratio averaged 5.6% with a peak of 22.1%, and inventory and orders averaged 8.2% and 8.5% with peaks of 33.8%.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-339e046bc70e",
    "ev-da66dff6a849",
    "ev-8f96d035e362"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "timeline": [
  {
   "time": "2026-10-24T00:12:47Z",
   "event": "First error logs appear: inventory 'connection reset by peer', orders 'inventory reservation failed with status 500', and gateway 'checkout failed: orders returned 502'.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-c30708431859",
    "ev-a57a947e1357",
    "ev-01577e4a4821"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-24T00:13:02Z",
   "event": "The 5xx ratio first reaches 5% or more on inventory, orders and gateway.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-da66dff6a849",
    "ev-8f96d035e362",
    "ev-339e046bc70e"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-24T00:14:13Z",
   "event": "First sampled error trace showing the path gateway 502 <- orders 502 <- inventory POST /reserve 500.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-a54c7699226e"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-24T00:14:46Z",
   "event": "Last error logs and last sampled error trace. By the end of the window the error ratio on all three services is 0.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-a54c7699226e",
    "ev-c30708431859",
    "ev-339e046bc70e",
    "ev-da66dff6a849",
    "ev-8f96d035e362"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "A latency or timeout cascade is unlikely. Failing traces completed in 7-39ms, no service had a p95 latency onset, and peak p95 stayed low (gateway 195ms, inventory 47ms).",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-a54c7699226e",
    "ev-339e046bc70e",
    "ev-da66dff6a849",
    "ev-8f96d035e362"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Gateway and orders are not where the errors start. Their errors only relay the downstream status, and the trace error path ends at inventory POST /reserve (500).",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-a54c7699226e",
    "ev-01577e4a4821",
    "ev-a57a947e1357"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "A traffic surge is unlikely. Gateway request rate averaged 2.02 req/s with a maximum of 2.28 req/s.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-339e046bc70e"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "Which peer reset inventory's connections (for example a database, cache or downstream service). There is no evidence from that dependency or from the network layer.",
  "Whether a deploy or configuration change happened. The deployment source was queried and returned no records for the window, which does not rule out changes made outside that system or before the window.",
  "Whether this will recur. The error ratio was 0 at the end of the window, but what stopped the resets is unknown.",
  "Whether inventory's connection pool, keepalive or idle-timeout settings are mismatched with the peer. A pattern like that would produce intermittent resets."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Open the example traces (7db1e2f7d552f9dd61f8e03aea9f083a, aff3d6150ea8122f3b8fe7b11a9c3cba) and the inventory logs around 00:12:47-00:14:46Z to find which outbound connection was reset.",
   "rationale": "This is the only way to identify the failing dependency behind 'connection reset by peer'.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-c30708431859",
    "ev-a54c7699226e"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Check health, restart and failover events, and connection limits on inventory's datastore and other dependencies between 00:12 and 00:15Z.",
   "rationale": "Brief, fast connection resets that clear on their own fit a peer restart, failover or connection-limit event.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-c30708431859",
    "ev-da66dff6a849"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Check for infrastructure or config changes outside the deployment system, such as network policy, load balancer or database maintenance.",
   "rationale": "The deployment source returned nothing for the window, so a change cannot be excluded from that source alone.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "src-deployments"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Consider adding retry-on-reset with connection validation in inventory for POST /reserve, if it is idempotent.",
   "rationale": "Every reset produced a user-facing checkout failure all the way up to gateway.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-c30708431859",
    "ev-a57a947e1357",
    "ev-01577e4a4821"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
